        "original_id": "db9e9229-7946-510a-9e77-92527de4d95e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jean-Baptiste Lully, Philippe Quinault, Louis XIV, Ovid\n- Works and Genres: Thésée, tragédie en musique, Metamorphoses\n\nFacts:\n- Jean-Baptiste Lully was born Giovanni Battista Lulli on 28 November 1632 and later became an Italian-born French composer, instrumentalist, and dancer.\n- Jean-Baptiste Lully spent most of his life working at the court of Louis XIV of France.\n- Tragédie en musique, also called tragédie lyrique, is a genre of French opera introduced by Jean-Baptiste Lully.\n- Jean-Baptiste Lully's followers used tragédie en musique until the second half of the eighteenth century.\n- Thésée is a tragédie en musique in a prologue and five acts.\n- Thésée has music by Jean-Baptiste Lully and a libretto by Philippe Quinault.\n- Thésée is based on Ovid's Metamorphoses.\n- Jean-Baptiste Lully died on 22 March 1687.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
